xnu 0139: try every AVDD/reset level and both read framings

The read-back through the ACTIVE TCS says the rail is enabled at 1800 mV, and
MISO returns zeros with a pull-down and ones with a pull-up, so nothing drives
it: the part is not running, or it never accepted the frame.

Two lines are left, AVDD (GPIO71) and reset (GPIO20), and their polarity is
only inferable from the vendor binary. Try all four level combinations, 150 ms
apart, and read the 0x10000 echo after each one, with the IRQ level printed
alongside.

The echo is read with both framings goodix_core.ko carries: the standard one
(0xF1, address, 00 00 FF) and the "bra" one (0xF1, address, four 0xFF bytes).
Whichever combination answers is the wiring, in one boot instead of eight.

